================================================================================
Bundled in the binary release archives
================================================================================

The dmem binary also has AWS-LC compiled in (through the aws-lc-rs and
aws-lc-sys crates), which provides its TLS cryptography, including the
post-quantum hybrid key exchange. AWS-LC is a fork of BoringSSL, itself a fork
of OpenSSL: new AWS-LC code is licensed Apache-2.0 OR ISC, and code from
BoringSSL and OpenSSL keeps its original ISC, Apache-2.0 or OpenSSL/SSLeay
licence. The release archives carry its full licence text as
THIRD-PARTY-aws-lc.txt. They also carry THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md, the licence text
of each Rust crate compiled into dmem; the file says which build and targets it
covers.

The prebuilt release archives ship the zvec native library (libzvec_c_api,
https://github.com/alibaba/zvec) next to the dmem binary. It is not part of
this source tree. zvec is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the
same text as LICENSE), and the library has Apache Arrow (also Apache License,
Version 2.0) built in. The attribution notices from their NOTICE files follow.

